{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787080255,"nonce":"F4bHk2+a/dGy2YOQWBlbkg8mnjQ=","title":"`MinDigestFloor` is a bound in name only, so `digest_floor: 0` passes the validator that exists to stop it and fails as a 23514 the operator has to decode","message":"**What is wrong.** `MinDigestFloor = 1` is declared at `internal/notification/domain/digest.go:31-33` with a reason — *\"send if anything at all happened. Zero is not a floor but a request to send for an empty window, which never happens\"* — and it is read by nothing. `validateDigest` (`internal/notification/domain/policy.go:459`) tests `p.Digest.Floor \u003c 0 || p.Digest.Floor \u003e MaxDigestFloor`. `MaxDigestFloor` is consulted; `MinDigestFloor` is not, and its sibling `MinDigestWindow` is (`:434`). Zero therefore passes a validator whose message says, in the same breath, *\"the digest floor is 1 to 10000, or unset\"*.\n\n**The demonstration.** The database disagrees. `policies_digest_floor_ck` (`db/migrations/00058_a_digest_is_a_window_over_a_namespace.sql:239-240`) is `CHECK (digest_floor IS NULL OR digest_floor BETWEEN 1 AND 10000)`, under a comment making the same argument the Go constant makes: *\"Zero is not admitted: it would mean 'send for an empty window', and an empty window sends nothing by construction, so the value would describe a behaviour that does not exist.\"*\n\n`PATCH` a policy with `{\"digest_floor\": 0}` and the two disagree in production. The patch DTO's `DigestFloor` is a `NullableInt32` with **no validate tag at all** (`internal/notification/api/dto.go:349`), so layer 1 sees nothing; `mapper.go:297-303` reads `Set` true and a non-nil `Value`, giving `p.DigestFloor = \u0026(\u00260)`; `validate.go:111-117` folds that onto `merged.Digest.Floor = 0`; `merged.Validate()` returns no violation. The write then reaches `internal/notification/repository/config.go:331-333`, where `p.DigestFloor != nil` sets `setFloor = true` and `floorVal = 0`, and Postgres refuses with a 23514 on `policies_digest_floor_ck`.\n\nThat is precisely the failure `validateDigest` was written to prevent. Its own doc comment (`policy.go:421-424`) states the job: *\"restates policies_digest_window_ck, policies_digest_floor_ck, policies_digest_pair_ck and policies_digest_reason_ck in Go, so that a bad digest comes back as a field-level violation the settings form can point at rather than as a 23514 an operator has to decode.\"* It names `policies_digest_floor_ck` and then does not restate its lower bound.\n\n**Why it matters.** A 23514 is a 500 with a constraint name in it. The operator gets no field path, so the settings form has no control to highlight, and the violation message the form was built around never arrives. The gap is narrow — a floor of exactly zero on the patch path — but it is narrow in the way that makes it survive: the create DTO carries `validate:\"omitempty,min=1,max=10000\"` (`dto.go:323`), so anyone testing the obvious path sees the right error and concludes the bound is enforced. The declared constant makes it worse rather than better, because a reader finds `MinDigestFloor = 1` sitting next to `MinDigestWindow` and reasonably assumes both are consulted.\n\n**Where.** `internal/notification/domain/digest.go:31-33` (`MinDigestFloor`, declared and unread) · `internal/notification/domain/policy.go:421-424` (the doc comment stating the contract), `:459` (the check that omits it), `:434` (`MinDigestWindow`, the sibling that is consulted) · `internal/notification/api/dto.go:349` (the patch DTO with no tag), `:323` (the create DTO that has one) · `internal/notification/api/mapper.go:297-303` and `internal/notification/api/validate.go:111-117` (how the zero survives to the domain) · `internal/notification/repository/config.go:331-333` (where it becomes a non-null 0) · `db/migrations/00058_a_digest_is_a_window_over_a_namespace.sql:235-240` (the constraint and its reasoning).\n\n**Scope.** small.\n\n**Done when.** `validateDigest` consults `MinDigestFloor`, so the admissible set it enforces is exactly the one `policies_digest_floor_ck` enforces — unset, or 1 through 10000 — and `{\"digest_floor\": 0}` on `PATCH` returns a field-level violation on `digest_floor` rather than a 23514. A test asserts the zero case on the patch path specifically, since the create path's DTO tag already covers it and is the reason this survived. No constant in `digest.go` is declared without a reader.","files":null}]}